{
  "conclusions": [
    "Independent per-packet +/-2ms propagation jitter creates roughly 45-50% media packet reordering in this workload. Preserve this as stress evidence, do not assume it represents typical Wi-Fi.",
    "At constant20Mbps with independent jitter, the link dropped no media/RTX datagrams yet forwarded 26394 RTX datagrams. FIFO delivery markedly reduced RTX; not a decrypted packet-to-original association or proof of zero endpoint kernel loss.",
    "FIFO constant-bandwidth runs still show about1.56-1.64s resume P95. Large delta frames burst near motion onset. Correcting the stale FPS expectation did not eliminate burst/latency and was reverted.",
    "Original protocol and acceptance thresholds unchanged. Alternate diagnostics are explicitly not original acceptance; step5 and image-quality/device regressions remain incomplete."
  ],
